# manual checks of sign-in (Rider, Visual Studio or the VS Code REST Client); the seed makes the accounts bob and
# room-101 with the password Seed__UserPassword of .env, and their clients Bob-Phone, Bob-Laptop, Bob-Smartwatch
# (bob), Room-101-Computer-01 and Room-101-Computer-02 (room-101); the clientId of a client is in the answer of
# GET /account/clients; the cookie of the panel is Secure, so use the https profile of the api
@host = https://localhost:7105
@password = change-me-1
@clientId = paste-the-client-id
@code = paste-a-code
@refreshToken = paste-a-refresh-token
@accessToken = paste-an-access-token

### sign in the account panel: the answer sets the cookie dara.account (no token in the body)
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "login": "bob", "password": "{{password}}" }

### the panel creates a registration code for a new client (10 minutes, used once)
POST {{host}}/account/clients/registration-code

### the app of the new client registers itself with the code: client tokens and the client id; an empty name gets
### "Phone 1", "PC 2"...
POST {{host}}/auth/register-client
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "{{code}}", "type": "Phone", "name": "Bob-Phone-2" }

### the panel issues a login code for an existing client (a copy of the app on another computer)
POST {{host}}/account/clients/{{clientId}}/login-code

### the existing client signs in with the login code; the tokens of its earlier copy end
POST {{host}}/auth/client-login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "{{code}}" }

### refresh the client tokens: the old refresh token is used up
POST {{host}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}" }

### sign out the client
POST {{host}}/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### sign out the panel: the session ends and the cookie is removed
POST {{host}}/auth/logout
